r Central Asia, Korasan and Afganistan from the Sassanian and Kushan Kingdoms. They continued to expand until the sixth century, when they were defeated by a recovered Sassasian Empire fighting alongside another confederation of central Asian nomads known as the Gokturks. This defeat destroyed Hepthalite power in transoxania, though some fragment of power seems to have existed until the Arab invasions.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 931, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 813})
