iberia) by the classical world and Kartli by the Georgians. Less well known but historically a part of Georgia is an area lying to the southwest of Imereti, in the valleys of the Chorokhi and the upper Kura, a land referred to as Zemo Kartli (Upper Iberia) or Meskhia. The lands to the south of the Kura but east of Upper Iberia are sometimes referred to as Kvemo Kartli (Lower Iberia), while the lands to the north, on the otherside of the Kura, are called Shida Kartli (Inner Iberia)."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1000, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 901})
